
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
CA = CB [00]
B,C,A are collinear [01]
CD = CA [02]
∠DBA = ∠EBD [03]
F,A,E are collinear [04]
FA = FE [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
G : Points
G,D,A are collinear [06]
B,G,E are collinear [07]

 * Proof steps:
001. F,A,E are collinear [04] & FA = FE [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of AE [08]
002. CD = CA [02] & CA = CB [00] ⇒  C is the circumcenter of \Delta BDA [09]
003. C is the circumcenter of \Delta BDA [09] & B,C,A are collinear [01] ⇒  BD ⟂ AD [10]
004. G,D,A are collinear [06] & BD ⟂ AD [10] ⇒  ∠GDB = ∠BDA [11]
005. B,G,E are collinear [07] & ∠EBD = ∠DBA [03] ⇒  ∠GBD = ∠DBA [12]
006. ∠GDB = ∠BDA [11] & ∠GBD = ∠DBA [12] (Similar Triangles)⇒  DG = DA [13]
007. G,D,A are collinear [06] & DG = DA [13] ⇒  D is midpoint of AG [14]
008. F is midpoint of AE [08] & D is midpoint of AG [14] ⇒  FD ∥ EG [15]
009. FD ∥ EG [15] & B,G,E are collinear [07] ⇒  DF ∥ BE
==========================
